ROOT CAUSE (code-level, not a seeder/data-shape defect):
VendorApp/lib/features/disbursement/domain/models/disbursement_report_model.dart:3-4 declares
`String? limit; String? offset;` and line 24 assigns `limit = json['limit'];` with no cast.
Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/Vendor/ReportController.php:83-84 (disbursement_report()) has
ALWAYS sent `'limit' => $limit` / `'offset' => $offset` as PHP ints (explicit `(int)` cast at
line 69-70), never strings -- this is a pre-existing client/server type contract mismatch that
predates NEARS-3499. It was unreachable and therefore silent before this ticket, because
business_settings.disbursement_type defaulted to 'manual' (Disbursement menu entry hidden) and
disbursements had 0 rows DB-wide -- this exact code path (a NON-EMPTY get-disbursement-report
response) was never exercised on a live device before NEARS-3499's fixture made it reachable.

IMPACT: DisbursementController.getDisbursementReport's try/catch (or lack thereof) leaves the
screen in a permanently blank state below the "Disbursement" app-bar title -- no rows, no status
badges, no error message shown to the vendor. Confirmed via accessibility dump: 13 nodes total,
only 1 labelled (the app-bar title "Disbursement"); body is empty.

This blocks NEARS-3499 AC2 (3 disbursement rows w/ status badges) and, transitively, AC3
(payment-info dialog reachable from a disbursement row) and NEARS-3486's corresponding
"Disbursement screen (3 status badges + Not Found fallback)" sub-flow, since the row list never
renders to tap into.
